    data: `<p><b>Slide content</b> (10 slides). Candidates who carried out their own research replace the sample findings with their group’s real data.</p><table style="border:1px solid #999"><thead><tr><th>Slide</th><th>Heading</th><th>On-slide text</th><th>Visual</th><th>Speaker notes – key points</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td><b>Filing Systems in Georgetown Offices</b></td><td><ul><li>Manual or Electronic?</li><li>Your name · your school</li><li>November 2026</li></ul></td><td>Photograph of filing cabinets beside a laptop</td><td>Introduce yourself and the topic; explain that every office must store and retrieve records.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td><b>Introduction</b></td><td><ul><li>Manual: paper files in cabinets</li><li>Electronic: drives, folders and files</li><li>Records must be retained and secured</li></ul></td><td>Image of a folder hierarchy diagram</td><td>Define manual and electronic filing and refer to retention and security from Section VIII.</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td><b>Research Questions</b></td><td><ul><li>Which filing systems are used?</li><li>How long does retrieval take?</li><li>What problems do offices face?</li></ul></td><td>Question-mark icon</td><td>Read the three research questions and explain their relevance.</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td><b>Purpose of the Research</b></td><td><ul><li>Compare the two systems in real offices</li><li>Identify problems and good practice</li><li>Advise offices on improvements</li></ul></td><td>Target icon</td><td>State the purpose and who benefits.</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td><b>Method of Investigation</b></td><td><ul><li>Qualitative: interviews and observation</li><li>Purposive sample of 6 offices</li><li>2 law, 2 medical, 2 real estate</li><li>Retrieval of one file timed in each office</li></ul></td><td>Image of an interview or a stopwatch</td><td>Justify the qualitative method and describe how the offices were chosen and visited.</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td><b>Filing Systems Used</b></td><td><ul><li>3 of 6 offices use both systems</li><li>Only 1 office is fully electronic</li></ul></td><td>Pie chart (system data)</td><td>Explain the mix of systems and why many offices are moving gradually to electronic filing.</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td><b>Time to Retrieve a File</b></td><td><ul><li>Manual: 6.5 minutes on average</li><li>Electronic: under 1 minute</li></ul></td><td>Column chart (retrieval times)</td><td>Compare the times and link to the advantages of electronic filing.</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td><b>Problems Reported</b></td><td><ul><li>Lack of storage space (5 of 6)</li><li>Misfiled folders (4 of 6)</li><li>No backup of scanned files (3 of 6)</li></ul></td><td>Bar chart (problem data)</td><td>Discuss each problem and which filing system it affects most.</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td><b>Recommendations and Conclusion</b></td><td><ul><li>Scan and index older files</li><li>Back up scanned files weekly</li><li>Electronic filing is faster but needs backups</li></ul></td><td>Checklist icon</td><td>Give two recommendations and the implementation strategy, then the conclusion.</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td><b>References</b></td><td><ul><li>Sources listed in APA style</li><li>Image credits</li></ul></td><td>None</td><td>Thank the offices that took part and invite questions.</td></tr></tbody></table><p><b>Sample findings for the chart slides</b></p><p><b>Slide 6 – Filing system used</b> (pie chart; total 6 offices, n = 6)</p><table style="border:1px solid #999"><thead><tr><th>Response</th><th>Number</th><th>Percentage</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Manual only</td><td>2</td><td>33.3%</td></tr><tr><td>Both manual and electronic</td><td>3</td><td>50%</td></tr><tr><td>Electronic only</td><td>1</td><td>16.7%</td></tr></tbody></table><p><b>Slide 7 – Average time to retrieve a requested file</b> (column chart, minutes)</p><table style="border:1px solid #999"><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Average time (minutes)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Manual</td><td>6.5</td></tr><tr><td>Manual and electronic</td><td>3.0</td></tr><tr><td>Electronic</td><td>0.75</td></tr></tbody></table><p><b>Slide 8 – Problems reported</b> (bar chart; more than one problem could be reported, n = 6)</p><table style="border:1px solid #999"><thead><tr><th>Response</th><th>Number</th><th>Percentage</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Lack of storage space</td><td>5</td><td>83.3%</td></tr><tr><td>Misfiled folders</td><td>4</td><td>66.7%</td></tr><tr><td>No backup of scanned files</td><td>3</td><td>50%</td></tr><tr><td>Damage from humidity or pests</td><td>2</td><td>33.3%</td></tr></tbody></table>`,
