    title: 'Presenting research on student backup and password habits',
    org: 'EDPM research group – student digital safety study',
    brief: `<p>Your group surveyed 40 Form 4 and Form 5 students about how they back up schoolwork and protect their accounts (see research brief research-4). Prepare an individual presentation of eight to ten slides for a Form assembly, encouraging students to protect their SBA work.</p>`,
    data: `<p><b>Slide content</b> (10 slides). Candidates who carried out their own research replace the sample findings with their group’s real data.</p><table style="border:1px solid #999"><thead><tr><th>Slide</th><th>Heading</th><th>On-slide text</th><th>Visual</th><th>Speaker notes – key points</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td><b>Back It Up! Student Backup and Password Habits</b></td><td><ul><li>EDPM Research Presentation</li><li>Your name · your school</li><li>November 2026</li></ul></td><td>Cloud-and-padlock icon</td><td>Introduce the topic and ask the audience how many have ever lost schoolwork.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td><b>Introduction</b></td><td><ul><li>Lost work means missed SBA deadlines</li><li>Backups and strong passwords protect files</li><li>Section VIII: file integrity and security</li></ul></td><td>Image of a broken laptop or USB drive</td><td>Explain why backups and passwords matter and refer to the syllabus content on security of files.</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td><b>Research Questions</b></td><td><ul><li>How often do students back up?</li><li>What password habits do they have?</li><li>How many have lost work, and why?</li></ul></td><td>Question-mark icon</td><td>Read each question and say why it was chosen.</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td><b>Purpose of the Research</b></td><td><ul><li>Measure current habits</li><li>Find the main risks</li><li>Plan a digital-safety campaign</li></ul></td><td>Target icon</td><td>State why the study was done and how the school will use it.</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td><b>Method of Investigation</b></td><td><ul><li>Quantitative survey</li><li>Anonymous questionnaire, 14 items</li><li>Stratified random sample of 40</li><li>20 Form 4 and 20 Form 5 students</li></ul></td><td>Questionnaire image</td><td>Justify the method and explain stratified random sampling by form.</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td><b>How Often Students Back Up</b></td><td><ul><li>35% never back up</li><li>Only 15% back up weekly</li></ul></td><td>Pie chart (backup frequency)</td><td>Explain the chart; point out that 25 of 40 students rarely or never back up.</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td><b>Password Habits</b></td><td><ul><li>55% use one password for everything</li><li>30% use two-step verification</li></ul></td><td>Column chart (password data)</td><td>Discuss the risks of reusing and sharing passwords.</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td><b>Lost Schoolwork</b></td><td><ul><li>42.5% have lost schoolwork</li><li>Cloud is the most used backup (15 of 26)</li></ul></td><td>Column chart (backup location)</td><td>Link lost work to the low backup rate and explain where the 26 students who back up keep their copies.</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td><b>Recommendations and Conclusion</b></td><td><ul><li>Weekly cloud backup reminder before SBA deadlines</li><li>Workshop on strong passwords and two-step verification</li><li>Most students are at risk of losing work</li></ul></td><td>Checklist icon</td><td>Give the recommendations and implementation strategy and conclude.</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td><b>References</b></td><td><ul><li>Sources listed in APA style</li><li>Image credits</li></ul></td><td>None</td><td>Thank the participants and invite questions.</td></tr></tbody></table><p><b>Sample findings for the chart slides</b></p><p><b>Slide 6 – How often students back up schoolwork</b> (pie chart; one answer each, total 40, n = 40)</p><table style="border:1px solid #999"><thead><tr><th>Response</th><th>Number</th><th>Percentage</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Never</td><td>14</td><td>35%</td></tr><tr><td>Rarely</td><td>11</td><td>27.5%</td></tr><tr><td>Monthly</td><td>9</td><td>22.5%</td></tr><tr><td>Weekly</td><td>6</td><td>15%</td></tr></tbody></table><p><b>Slide 7 – Password practices</b> (column chart; separate yes/no items, n = 40)</p><table style="border:1px solid #999"><thead><tr><th>Response</th><th>Number</th><th>Percentage</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Same password for all accounts</td><td>22</td><td>55%</td></tr><tr><td>Have shared a password with a friend</td><td>9</td><td>22.5%</td></tr><tr><td>Use two-step verification</td><td>12</td><td>30%</td></tr></tbody></table><p><b>Slide 8 – Where the 26 students who back up keep their backups</b> (column chart; total 26, n = 26)</p><table style="border:1px solid #999"><thead><tr><th>Response</th><th>Number</th><th>Percentage</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cloud storage</td><td>15</td><td>57.7%</td></tr><tr><td>USB flash drive</td><td>8</td><td>30.8%</td></tr><tr><td>External hard drive</td><td>3</td><td>11.5%</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Students who have lost schoolwork because of a device failure, loss or theft: 17 of 40 (42.5%).</p>`,
